WEBVTT

00:02.254 --> 00:07.181
<i>The Roundtable members hold
their own even against Victor, the most powerful man.</i>

00:07.641 --> 00:13.527
<i>However, the regeneration and combat skills
far surpassing that of Andy prevents their victory.</i>

00:14.111 --> 00:17.827
<i>But in order to bring Andy back,
Fuko returns with the Card in hand,</i>

00:17.827 --> 00:20.040
<i>getting close to Victor to change the tide.</i>

00:20.415 --> 00:24.173
<i>Fuko makes physical contact with Victor
to create a stroke of unluck,</i>

00:24.173 --> 00:26.177
<i>and Juiz comes up with a plan-</i>

00:26.302 --> 00:30.143
<i>to bring back Andy's consciousness
as Fuko has a high affinity for him,</i>

00:30.435 --> 00:33.693
<i>so that a giant stroke of unluck can be affixed
to Victor in an instant.</i>

00:34.611 --> 00:37.617
<i>In order to deliver her voice to Andy,
Fuko opens a hole in Victor's forehead</i>

00:37.617 --> 00:39.955
<i>where the Card was lodged and begins to shout.</i>

00:40.540 --> 00:44.422
<i>Fuko's desperate words miraculously awakens
Andy's consciousness,</i>

00:44.715 --> 00:46.844
<i>and a gigantic stroke of unluck rains down.</i>

00:47.762 --> 00:52.396
<i>Fuko wakes up in a hospital room...
and Andy in his usual guise is sitting next to her.</i>

00:53.023 --> 00:59.327
<i>Fuko sheds tears of joy and relief...
but now, Apocalypse opens once again.</i>

01:27.967 --> 01:31.182
Fascinating. You really are "Unseen".

01:31.934 --> 01:35.399
You're a self-targeting compulsory activation-type.

01:35.775 --> 01:42.371
When you shut your eyes, your body and anything
you recognize as your property become invisible.

01:46.254 --> 01:51.139
But that's odd.
That's your blood coming from your stomach.

01:51.682 --> 01:53.101
Maybe you didn't notice?

01:54.353 --> 01:59.238
I don't want you running off on me,
so I cut open your stomach and put a homing device in there.

01:59.614 --> 02:02.579
If you join us,
then I'll deactivate my ability.

02:03.455 --> 02:08.006
If you don't, then that wound won't heal until I'm dead.

02:09.300 --> 02:10.260
Unseen...

02:11.262 --> 02:15.897
You're mine.
I'm not gonna hand you over to those guys.

04:04.365 --> 04:06.829
QUESTS ENDED

04:06.829 --> 04:09.333
SEPTEMBER 1ST

04:09.333 --> 04:11.797
INSIDE UNION FACILITY-
THE ROUNDTABLE

04:37.724 --> 04:41.690
Everyone is assembled, then.
Proceed, Apocalypse.

04:42.859 --> 04:44.028
Yes.

04:44.946 --> 04:47.744
Quest results!

04:56.052 --> 04:56.804
Huh?

04:56.804 --> 04:59.475
Wait, is today August 31st?

05:04.778 --> 05:06.322
Have I been asleep for that long?

05:06.782 --> 05:08.536
Well, yeah, that's a no-brainer.

05:08.536 --> 05:11.542
A total shut-in movin' around like that?
It was bound to shut your body down.

05:23.189 --> 05:30.370
I declare to those sitting at the Roundtable.
The results of the six quests given to you-

05:30.830 --> 05:36.967
Item One: Capture of UMA Burn...
Successful.

05:37.552 --> 05:38.512
Participants...

05:39.013 --> 05:43.981
Juiz, Tatiana, Billy...

05:45.150 --> 05:49.951
...Isshin, Phil, Top.

05:50.493 --> 05:54.043
Reward: Addition of an eleventh seat.

05:57.508 --> 06:02.392
One more Negator may be added to the Roundtable.

06:05.858 --> 06:12.538
Item Two: Capture of the UMA Eat...
Successful.

06:12.789 --> 06:18.341
Participants: Juiz, Tatiana...

06:18.717 --> 06:23.560
...Billy, Phil, Top.

06:33.121 --> 06:37.296
Reward: Location of Negator Unburn.

06:38.966 --> 06:43.559
I will reveal their exact location
for the next seven days.

06:43.559 --> 06:49.946
Unburn is currently here.
They won't detect that they've been marked.

06:49.946 --> 06:57.252
Catch them if you need them.
Though you probably don't as you've already captured Burn.

06:58.296 --> 07:05.226
Item Three: Neutralization of UMA Language...
Successful.

07:05.936 --> 07:09.151
Participant: Nico Vorgeil.

07:09.778 --> 07:13.702
Reward: Unification of all the world's languages.

07:38.292 --> 07:42.217
Altering the memories and cultures
of all non-Negators.

07:42.217 --> 07:45.056
All languages have now been unified to English.

07:46.810 --> 07:48.271
Mui dear, do you read me?

07:48.564 --> 07:52.697
Hm. Yes, sir?
Master Shen, is something the matter?

07:53.156 --> 07:54.784
Are you wearing your necktie right now?

07:56.120 --> 07:59.334
No, sir. I'm in the middle
of training at the moment.

07:59.627 --> 08:02.299
Ah, I see. Perfect timing.

08:04.219 --> 08:06.473
I'D LOVE SOME OF
YOUR DIM SUM TODAY.
Wo jīntiān yào páo ni de dianxīn.

08:06.473 --> 08:07.142
HOW ABOUT IT?
Zěnme yàng?

08:09.564 --> 08:14.824
E-Er, what did you just say, sir?
Would you mind repeating it once again?

08:15.241 --> 08:18.707
<i>No, that's all I needed.
Sorry. Catch you later!</i>

08:18.707 --> 08:22.005
U-Uh, yes... understood, sir.

08:26.556 --> 08:28.769
Confirmed unification of languages.

08:29.687 --> 08:35.866
Item Four: Capture of the UMA Past...
Successful.

08:36.743 --> 08:41.920
Participants: Juiz, Nico, Phil.

08:42.337 --> 08:47.389
Reward: Artifact Rebellion is here.

08:48.349 --> 08:56.031
And Item Five:
Capture of the UMA Spoil... Successful.

08:58.578 --> 09:04.214
Participants: Andy, Fuko.

09:04.214 --> 09:05.634
Y-Yes!

09:06.720 --> 09:08.139
Shen.

09:08.431 --> 09:14.192
Reward: Location of Negator Unrepair.

09:14.276 --> 09:20.455
We did it! There's Unrepair, Andy!
They might just be able to give you an actual death!

09:23.920 --> 09:30.934
Item Six: Capture of Negator Unseen...
Failed.

09:35.443 --> 09:37.322
How very unfortunate.

09:37.657 --> 09:38.533
Huh?

09:38.950 --> 09:40.704
We had an inkling.

09:41.163 --> 09:44.378
The guys that went
to investigate Unseen all died.

09:44.921 --> 09:49.137
<i>Their bound bodies ended up in
a deserted area, and all of 'em...</i>

09:49.304 --> 09:50.724
<i>...bled to death.</i>

09:53.396 --> 09:57.738
My guess is Unseen got taken by Unrepair.

10:04.836 --> 10:07.633
All quests have not been cleared.

10:07.633 --> 10:09.971
Therefore, you shall receive a penalty.

10:09.971 --> 10:13.227
Now adding the UMA Galaxy!

10:30.011 --> 10:31.598
I-It's ginormous!

10:31.598 --> 10:33.434
What is this thing?

10:45.374 --> 10:46.794
So this thing is...

10:46.794 --> 10:48.673
The penalty, eh?

11:14.101 --> 11:16.773
Huh? It went up.

11:16.773 --> 11:18.234
Is it tryna get to the surface?

11:19.236 --> 11:19.946
Move.

11:21.533 --> 11:23.119
You call for me?

11:23.494 --> 11:26.083
Hey, Move!
Thanks for the other day, by the way!

11:29.089 --> 11:31.636
Ah! It's the thing
that brought us here!

11:32.597 --> 11:35.101
Move, transport us to the surface.

11:36.020 --> 11:36.855
All right.

11:38.901 --> 11:39.652
Huh?

11:40.529 --> 11:41.405
Oh...

11:49.254 --> 11:54.264
No!

11:57.062 --> 11:59.734
Galaxy has been added.

11:59.734 --> 12:03.324
A new Rule that the world
will believe has always existed.

12:04.744 --> 12:09.754
Will you be able to overcome this penalty, Negators?

12:20.609 --> 12:22.738
Andy, where are we?

12:22.738 --> 12:24.366
Australia, I figure.

12:24.575 --> 12:29.042
Oh! I've seen that rock before!
It's the biggest rock in the world, right?

12:29.334 --> 12:36.223
Juiz... I've done my part in transporting you all.
Now I expect to see quite the show.

12:36.599 --> 12:42.570
Yes... I understand, Move.
I shall give you a front-row seat to my justice.

12:51.921 --> 12:52.715
Hey.

12:52.715 --> 12:53.800
Hm?

12:54.217 --> 12:58.267
I thought this "penalty"
would be a lot scarier.

12:58.267 --> 12:59.520
But this doesn't seem so bad, does it?

13:00.271 --> 13:04.530
Negative. We're dealing with
a UMA added by Apocalypse.

13:04.530 --> 13:07.452
They always possess Rules
that lead humanity to ruin.

13:08.370 --> 13:10.416
This one is no exception.

13:11.043 --> 13:13.339
The alteration... is starting.

13:36.176 --> 13:37.137
Hm?

13:56.216 --> 13:57.970
What's that? Amazing!

13:57.970 --> 14:00.391
Hey, it's amazing, huh?!
Look at that! Hey!

14:00.391 --> 14:02.605
Nico, I want confirmation about this patch.

14:02.855 --> 14:04.065
Already on it.

14:06.153 --> 14:10.202
Hey, you dimwits, it's me!
A Rule was just added!

14:10.202 --> 14:15.589
What's common knowledge
to you isn't to us Negators!

14:15.589 --> 14:17.968
So, give me your knowledge now!

14:18.260 --> 14:20.431
- Roger, Dr. Nico!
- Roger, Dr. Nico!

14:21.058 --> 14:25.399
Times like this are the only times
when we're superior to Pappy!

14:26.109 --> 14:28.489
Quit saying that or you'll get killed.

14:54.040 --> 14:55.251
I see.

14:57.088 --> 15:00.679
This "galaxy" is a cluster
of celestial bodies like Earth.

15:01.054 --> 15:05.522
Basically, this penalty spawned
a slew of these Earth-like bodies,

15:05.981 --> 15:10.489
<i>along with systems involving them such
as myths and days of the week.</i>

15:10.489 --> 15:14.957
<i>It also introduced the concept
of extraterrestrial life-forms called aliens...</i>

15:15.082 --> 15:20.092
...and at this very moment,
seems like those aliens are invading us.

15:20.844 --> 15:23.600
- Awesome! So cool!
- Huh? What?

15:23.975 --> 15:26.480
What is that thing?
Are those ships flying in the sky?

15:27.190 --> 15:28.150
Are they enemies?

15:28.526 --> 15:35.498
Yeah. Born moments ago from the alteration
to a world that always had Galaxy.

15:35.498 --> 15:38.671
Naturally, that's not what they perceive.

15:41.886 --> 15:45.184
Born on a planet with several hundred
million years of history,

15:45.184 --> 15:48.190
they trained themselves for decades
to become soldiers,

15:48.608 --> 15:52.031
and were given ships
to invade other planets.

15:52.031 --> 15:56.414
With their own planet on a path to ruin,
they're looking for a new home, or something.

15:57.500 --> 16:00.005
I'd wager that's their backstory.

16:03.011 --> 16:05.266
We are Acks.

16:05.266 --> 16:10.317
We're invading this planet
to make it our new home world.

16:10.652 --> 16:11.946
See that?

16:11.946 --> 16:15.161
Y'don't say.
This is a penalty, all right.

16:16.747 --> 16:19.377
Is there a representative for this planet?

16:19.795 --> 16:20.881
Me.

16:22.926 --> 16:28.771
If you offer no resistance,
then we plan on using you as our labor force.

16:28.771 --> 16:31.484
You all seem to possess moderate intelligence.

16:32.069 --> 16:37.789
If you resist, you'll be a hinderance
and thus eliminated. Make your choice.

16:40.336 --> 16:43.342
I choose neither.
Withdraw your ships.

16:57.328 --> 17:02.839
We've done our research.
This planet's civilization is horribly underdeveloped.

17:03.298 --> 17:08.267
You've yet to make an advancement into space due
to your species' lack of cooperativeness.

17:08.475 --> 17:10.981
You cannot possibly win by force.

17:11.774 --> 17:18.120
This is genocide. In order for my family,
friends, and people to live on this planet...

17:18.120 --> 17:20.667
...all of you must die.

17:21.669 --> 17:23.923
Is that your vision of justice?

17:23.923 --> 17:28.558
Yes. A vision infallible to any form
of reasoning otherwise.

17:29.768 --> 17:30.854
I see.

17:32.649 --> 17:33.568
In that case, I'll just have to...

17:35.739 --> 17:38.285
...negate that justice.

17:42.295 --> 17:43.673
What was that?

17:46.596 --> 17:47.263
Wha?

17:52.190 --> 17:53.610
Gah! What's going on?

17:53.985 --> 17:56.824
Amazing. Seriously amazing!

18:24.839 --> 18:26.968
What did you just do!?

18:31.017 --> 18:33.105
Andy, Fuko.

18:33.105 --> 18:37.113
Observe closely.
This is what a penalty entails.

18:39.660 --> 18:42.708
We managed to avoid
the situation this time with my ability...

18:42.708 --> 18:45.922
...but depending on the member involved,
it could just as easily be game over.

18:46.507 --> 18:49.471
This marks the 99th penalty added.

18:50.264 --> 18:53.020
We cannot afford any more penalties.

18:56.485 --> 18:57.738
Why's that?

18:58.489 --> 19:01.495
We uncovered a stone tablet
at the same time as Apocalypse.

19:01.954 --> 19:08.551
That tablet has 101 slots.
Each time we receive a penalty, one slot gets filled.

19:10.137 --> 19:12.225
<i>There is only one open slot left until it reaches 100.</i>

19:13.185 --> 19:16.609
<i>Beyond that lies the final penalty.</i>

19:17.569 --> 19:18.822
<i>Ragnarøk.</i>

19:22.579 --> 19:25.000
I assume it's a word that denotes "the end."

19:25.334 --> 19:29.217
In order to protect this planet,
we must prevent that at all costs.

19:29.217 --> 19:33.141
That is why we resist,
no matter what quest comes our way.

19:35.062 --> 19:35.814
That said...

19:36.398 --> 19:41.032
<i>The quests-Apocalypse won't open unless
the Roundtable is fully occupied.</i>

19:48.798 --> 19:51.929
I get it!
Since we have another seat...

19:52.514 --> 19:53.390
Yes.

19:54.017 --> 19:59.862
We obtained an eleventh seat as a reward
for passing the Burn quest. Unless we fill it...

20:00.279 --> 20:05.957
...we'll receive a penalty in three months' time,
before we can take up any more quests.

20:06.626 --> 20:11.636
In other words, our highest priority right now
is securing an eleventh member.

20:12.261 --> 20:13.806
So this time we're...

20:14.390 --> 20:15.894
The hunters.

20:18.357 --> 20:21.530
You... all of you... just who are...

20:23.450 --> 20:25.245
You're still here?

20:25.245 --> 20:30.422
So you didn't kill yourself despite my power.
It seems your "vision" was tall talk after all.

20:31.383 --> 20:34.682
No matter.
Relay this message across space.

20:38.438 --> 20:40.735
Keep your hands off planet Earth.

20:53.720 --> 21:00.107
<i>On September 1st, 2020,
humanity made first contact with extraterrestrial life.</i>

21:00.482 --> 21:06.035
<i>However, it would be the first and last time,
as all contact would cease thereafter.</i>

21:13.091 --> 21:17.308
We've learned the whereabouts of Unburn
and Unrepair as our reward this time around.

21:17.768 --> 21:22.485
Reward: Location of Negator Unburn.

21:22.861 --> 21:27.244
Location of Unrepair.
Right here.

21:27.704 --> 21:28.539
The one we want is...

21:28.623 --> 21:30.627
Unrepair, right?

21:33.841 --> 21:39.268
I'll go. If their ability is true to their name,
one attack'll prove to be fatal.

21:39.603 --> 21:43.193
I appreciate that.
I'll assign you backup for insurance.

21:43.193 --> 21:45.865
Take Tatiana along with you.
She will prove helpful.

21:45.949 --> 21:47.409
Wait a-me?

21:48.411 --> 21:50.583
Fuko, you go along as well.

21:53.380 --> 21:57.931
Roger that. I gotta repay
the favor for helping me out!

22:01.772 --> 22:05.989
TO BE CONTINUED

23:36.002 --> 23:36.461
PREVIEW

23:36.879 --> 23:41.555
<i>The next destination for the undead man and the girl
is a lavish cruise boat in the south seas.</i>

23:41.555 --> 23:44.686
<i>What awaits there are individuals
with suspicious shadows.</i>

23:44.978 --> 23:48.569
<i>Next episode of Undead Unluck,
Episode 11-Rio de Janeiro.</i>

23:48.778 --> 23:50.948
<i>In search of the greatest death ever.</i>
